ian"],["az.diplomatic","Diplomatic corps","az.diplomatic",["013","D","004"],"Iranshahr","Azerbaijan","Mission code, class letter, serial — told apart by gaps, not hyphens.","AzerbaijanThemes.diplomatic"],["az.foreign","Foreign-owned company","az.foreign",["H","023","149"],"Iranshahr","Azerbaijan","The one coloured field that keeps the civilian black ink.","AzerbaijanThemes.foreign"],["af.car","Car","af.car",["12346","P","HRT"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","Private `ش`/`PRV`, duplicate `ش`/`DUPL`, taxi `ت`, bus `ب` and lorry `ل`, with three to five figures. Taxi and bus print on yellow.","AfghanistanThemes.civilian"],["af.kabul6","Kabul (six figures)","af.kabul6",["5","12346","P"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","Kabul exhausted five figures. The sixth is printed once, in Persian only, between two hyphens.","AfghanistanThemes.civilian"],["af.cycle","Motorcycle / rickshaw","af.cycle",["123","M","NRZ"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","Three figures with `م`/`M`, four with `ر`/`TRC`, on a shallower two-wheeler blank.","AfghanistanThemes.civilian"],["af.diplomatic","Diplomatic corps","af.diplomatic",["12","34","KBL"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","The only hyphenated Afghan number, and the only `CD` — printed once, with no Persian counterpart.","AfghanistanThemes.diplomatic"],["af.governmental","Governmental","af.governmental",["1234","KBL"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","A government vehicle's type is not printed: a dash stands in both registers.","AfghanistanThemes.governmental"],["af.un","United Nations","af.un",["1234","KBL"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","The plainest: the province block and the number, and nothing at the head.","AfghanistanThemes.un"],["af.temporary","Private temporary","af.temporary",["12346","HRT"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","Issued from 2023, valid three years. The one Afghan plate printed in two inks.","AfghanistanThemes.civilian"],["af.international","Cross-border (Herat, 2026)","af.international",["12346","B","HRT"],"Iranshahr","Afghanistan","Latin figures and a spelled-out category, no Persian half. Reconstructed from text — no photograph exists.","AfghanistanThemes.civilian"],["am.car","Private car","am.car",["01","AD","234"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The 2014 design: region code, two letters, three digits, and the silver band beside the flag.","ArmeniaThemes.civilian"],["am.carTwoRow","Private car (two-row)","am.carTwoRow",["01","AD","234"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The same seven characters in the same three groups, on a deeper canvas.","ArmeniaThemes.civilian"],["am.motorcycle","Motorcycle","am.motorcycle",["01","AD","234"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The two-row plate was found too cumbersome to carry; the gap between region and letters was closed.","ArmeniaThemes.civilian"],["am.public","State-owned (Security Council)","am.public",["001","NN","01"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The number reversed: `NN 01` names the institution, and only fourteen pairs are issued at all.","ArmeniaThemes.civilian"],["am.trailer","Trailer","am.trailer",["290","L","01"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","A pre-2014 design: no identifier band, and the letter count cut to one — most often `L`.","ArmeniaThemes.civilian"],["am.bus","Bus","am.bus",["1234","S"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The Soviet public-transport format Armenia kept: `S` for a city bus, `L` for a long-range coach.","ArmeniaThemes.bus"],["am.diplomatic","Diplomatic corps","am.diplomatic",["04","D","057","AM"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","Mission code, `D` for a diplomat or `T` for a technician, serial, and Armenia's own code at the tail: `AM`, or `ARM` on newer plates.","ArmeniaThemes.diplomatic"],["am.un","United Nations","am.un",["080"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","Three digits between two printed words. Nothing on this plate is chosen but the serial.","ArmeniaThemes.un"],["am.military","Ministry of Defence","am.military",["1007","M"],"Iranshahr","Armenia","The one Armenian plate with no Latin on it: `ՊՆ` for the ministry, `Մ` for a passenger vehicle, `Տ` for a transport one.","ArmeniaThemes.military"],["tj.car","Private car